  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mission Global African Hydrogen Summit 2024 Namibia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The combi-track &quot;Green Hydrogen&quot;(GH2) in Namibia and South Africa, aims to establish the Netherlands as a pivotal partner in transitioning towards a green and inclusive hydrogen sector, focusing on trade, investments, job creation, and skills development.Former Prime Minister Rutte&apos;s visit, along with accompanying businesses and the business forum, has significantly contributed to advancing these goals and laid the groundwork for future collaborations. The roundtable discussions held last year have identified concrete areas for further engagement.The goal of this project is to participate in the GH2 sector in Namibia and South Africa, with a Dutch delegation in exploring sustainable business opportunities.Attendance at the Global African Hydrogen Summit, combined with field visits and Business-to-Business (B2B) matchmaking, would expose Dutch businesses to potential partners in Namibia, creating the following opportunities:&#x2022;	Catalysing cooperation, exchange and partnerships between Dutch water management businesses and Namibian businesses, as well as governments and knowledge institutes, by bringing relevant actors together;&#x2022;	Offering Dutch businesses relevant insights in opportunities for projects and investments in Namibia;&#x2022;	Positioning the Netherlands as a frontrunner and partner in GH2;&#x2022;	Paving the way for future long lasting developments and cooperation in the entire value chain of green hydrogen between the private sector, as well as between national and local government;&#x2022;	Facilitating the next step in the opportunities identified during the visit of the former Prime Minister of the Netherlands in June 2023.</narrative>
  </description>
